.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/@nodelib/fs.walk Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "@nodelib/fs\&.walk"
.PP
.RS 4
A library for efficiently walking a directory recursively\&. 
.RE
.PP
.SH ":bulb: Highlights"
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
:moneybag: Returns useful information: \fRname\fP, \fRpath\fP, \fRdirent\fP and \fRstats\fP (optional)\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
:rocket: On Node\&.js 10\&.10+ uses the mechanism without additional calls to determine the entry type for performance reasons\&. See \fR\fRold\fP and \fRmodern\fP mode\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
:gear: Built-in directories/files and error filtering system\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
:link: Can safely work with broken symbolic links\&.
.PP
.SH "Install"
.PP
.PP
.nf
npm install @nodelib/fs\&.walk
.fi
.PP
.SH "Usage"
.PP
.PP
.nf
import * as fsWalk from '@nodelib/fs\&.walk';

fsWalk\&.walk('path', (error, entries) => { /* … */ });
.fi
.PP
.SH "API"
.PP
.SS "\&.walk(path, [optionsOrSettings], callback)"
Reads the directory recursively and asynchronously\&. Requires a callback function\&.

.PP
.RS 4
:book: If you want to use the Promise API, use \fRutil\&.promisify\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
.PP
.nf
fsWalk\&.walk('path', (error, entries) => { /* … */ });
fsWalk\&.walk('path', {}, (error, entries) => { /* … */ });
fsWalk\&.walk('path', new fsWalk\&.Settings(), (error, entries) => { /* … */ });
.fi
.PP
.SS "\&.walkStream(path, [optionsOrSettings])"
Reads the directory recursively and asynchronously\&. \fRReadable Stream\fP is used as a provider\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
const stream = fsWalk\&.walkStream('path');
const stream = fsWalk\&.walkStream('path', {});
const stream = fsWalk\&.walkStream('path', new fsWalk\&.Settings());
.fi
.PP
.SS "\&.walkSync(path, [optionsOrSettings])"
Reads the directory recursively and synchronously\&. Returns an array of entries\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
const entries = fsWalk\&.walkSync('path');
const entries = fsWalk\&.walkSync('path', {});
const entries = fsWalk\&.walkSync('path', new fsWalk\&.Settings());
.fi
.PP
.SS "path"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Required: \fRtrue\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: \fRstring | Buffer | URL\fP
.PP

.PP
A path to a file\&. If a URL is provided, it must use the \fRfile:\fP protocol\&.
.SS "optionsOrSettings"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Required: \fRfalse\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: \fROptions | Settings\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Default: An instance of \fRSettings\fP class
.PP

.PP
An \fB`Options`\fP object or an instance of \fB`Settings`\fP class\&.

.PP
.RS 4
:book: When you pass a plain object, an instance of the \fRSettings\fP class will be created automatically\&. If you plan to call the method frequently, use a pre-created instance of the \fRSettings\fP class\&. 
.RE
.PP
.SS "Settings([options])"
A class of full settings of the package\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
const settings = new fsWalk\&.Settings({ followSymbolicLinks: true });

const entries = fsWalk\&.walkSync('path', settings);
.fi
.PP
.SH "Entry"
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRname\fP — The name of the entry (\fRunknown\&.txt\fP)\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRpath\fP — The path of the entry relative to call directory (\fRroot/unknown\&.txt\fP)\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRdirent\fP — An instance of \fR\fRfs\&.Dirent\fP\fP class\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
[\fRstats\fP] — An instance of \fRfs\&.Stats\fP class\&.
.PP
.SH "Options"
.PP
.SS "basePath"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: \fRstring\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Default: \fRundefined\fP
.PP

.PP
By default, all paths are built relative to the root path\&. You can use this option to set custom root path\&.

.PP
In the example below we read the files from the \fRroot\fP directory, but in the results the root path will be \fRcustom\fP\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
fsWalk\&.walkSync('root'); // → ['root/file\&.txt']
fsWalk\&.walkSync('root', { basePath: 'custom' }); // → ['custom/file\&.txt']
.fi
.PP
.SS "concurrency"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: \fRnumber\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Default: \fRInfinity\fP
.PP

.PP
The maximum number of concurrent calls to \fRfs\&.readdir\fP\&.

.PP
.RS 4
:book: The higher the number, the higher performance and the load on the File System\&. If you want to read in quiet mode, set the value to \fR4 * os\&.cpus()\&.length\fP (4 is default size of \fRthread pool work scheduling\fP)\&. 
.RE
.PP
.SS "deepFilter"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: \fR\fRDeepFilterFunction\fP\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Default: \fRundefined\fP
.PP

.PP
A function that indicates whether the directory will be read deep or not\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
// Skip all directories that starts with `node_modules`
const filter: DeepFilterFunction = (entry) => !entry\&.path\&.startsWith('node_modules');
.fi
.PP
.SS "entryFilter"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: \fR\fREntryFilterFunction\fP\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Default: \fRundefined\fP
.PP

.PP
A function that indicates whether the entry will be included to results or not\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
// Exclude all `\&.js` files from results
const filter: EntryFilterFunction = (entry) => !entry\&.name\&.endsWith('\&.js');
.fi
.PP
.SS "errorFilter"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: \fR\fRErrorFilterFunction\fP\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Default: \fRundefined\fP
.PP

.PP
A function that allows you to skip errors that occur when reading directories\&.

.PP
For example, you can skip \fRENOENT\fP errors if required:

.PP
.PP
.nf
// Skip all ENOENT errors
const filter: ErrorFilterFunction = (error) => error\&.code == 'ENOENT';
.fi
.PP
.SS "stats"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: \fRboolean\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Default: \fRfalse\fP
.PP

.PP
Adds an instance of \fRfs\&.Stats\fP class to the \fB`Entry`\fP\&.

.PP
.RS 4
:book: Always use \fRfs\&.readdir\fP with additional \fRfs\&.lstat/fs\&.stat\fP calls to determine the entry type\&. 
.RE
.PP
.SS "followSymbolicLinks"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: \fRboolean\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Default: \fRfalse\fP
.PP

.PP
Follow symbolic links or not\&. Call \fRfs\&.stat\fP on symbolic link if \fRtrue\fP\&.
.SS "\fRthrowErrorOnBrokenSymbolicLink\fP"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: \fRboolean\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Default: \fRtrue\fP
.PP

.PP
Throw an error when symbolic link is broken if \fRtrue\fP or safely return \fRlstat\fP call if \fRfalse\fP\&.
.SS "\fRpathSegmentSeparator\fP"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: \fRstring\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Default: \fRpath\&.sep\fP
.PP

.PP
By default, this package uses the correct path separator for your OS (\fR\\\fP on Windows, \fR/\fP on Unix-like systems)\&. But you can set this option to any separator character(s) that you want to use instead\&.
.SS "\fRfs\fP"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: \fRFileSystemAdapter\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Default: A default FS methods
.PP

.PP
By default, the built-in Node\&.js module (\fRfs\fP) is used to work with the file system\&. You can replace any method with your own\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
interface FileSystemAdapter {
    lstat: typeof fs\&.lstat;
    stat: typeof fs\&.stat;
    lstatSync: typeof fs\&.lstatSync;
    statSync: typeof fs\&.statSync;
    readdir: typeof fs\&.readdir;
    readdirSync: typeof fs\&.readdirSync;
}

const settings = new fsWalk\&.Settings({
    fs: { lstat: fakeLstat }
});
.fi
.PP
